    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **72 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS** (including the 4 new segment tests).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field following the project's existing pattern for read-time derived values (like `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `timezone`).\n\n**New logic** \u2014 `rest/function/common/OwnerSegments.java`:\n- `TIER` = `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3`, else `STANDARD` (using the stored level, falling back to `Membership.levelOf(owner)` \u2014 mirroring how the mapper resolves `membershipLevel`).\n- `AREA` = `METRO` when the owner's locality (`CustomerCodes.localityOf`) is a known region (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`), else `REGIONAL`.\n- Returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**Wiring**:\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 imported `OwnerSegments` and added `@Mapping(target = \"ownerSegment\", expression = \"java(OwnerSegments.of(owner))\")`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` string field to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it), documenting all four values and the TIER/AREA rules.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 `OwnerSegmentTests.java` exercises all four segments end-to-end via `POST /api/owners` + `GET`: `STANDARD_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `PREMIUM_METRO`, and `PREMIUM_REGIONAL` (the last two via a 3-member household whose third member reaches level 3).\n\nNo `@RestController`/Spring MVC was introduced \u2014 the change stays within the derived-field mapping layer, consistent with AGENTS.md.",
